          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Percy Bysshe Shelley's Birth and Upbringing</strong><br>\nPercy Bysshe Shelley was born in 1792 into a wealthy aristocratic family in Sussex, England. He was educated at Eton College, where he was known for his resistance to authority and interest in radical politics and science, which would influence his later works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>University Life and Expulsion</strong><br>\nShelley attended University College, Oxford, but his time there was brief. He was expelled for co-authoring \"The Necessity of Atheism,\" which challenged the existence of God. This expulsion marked the beginning of his lifelong commitment to social and political activism through his poetry.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Early Writing and First Marriage</strong><br>\nShelley published his first Gothic novel, \"Zastrozzi,\" at age 17, followed by several other works. In 1811, he eloped with Harriet Westbrook, a move that caused further estrangement from his family and society due to their difference in social standing and his abandonment of her later in their marriage.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
